  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nWhen dynamically importing a script, there's no way to tell the browser that the script is of lower priority, and avoid its contention with higher priority resources. The `import()` call doesn't have a way to express that.\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nToday, we can shim this by overriding import and use it to inject a top-level module that includes a `fetchpriority` attribute.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nAdding a `fetchpriority` keyword to `import()`'s options dictionary could enable that.\r\nIt remains to be seen if we need the same for static imports given the discussion in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10276\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
